amux workgroup — create, open and manage workgroups and their agents

usage: amux workgroup [<command>]
aliases: wg, session, ses, workspace, ws

Bare amux workgroup is the interactive create page (same as new).

commands:
  new [repo...]             interactive create page: coordinator harness/model and optional repos
  create <repo>... [flags]  non-interactive: a workgroup limited to those repos, with one agent on them
  repo <repo> [flags]       non-interactive: a workgroup limited to one repo, with one agent on it
  add <root> [repo...] [--agent a] [--mode m] [--model M] [--prompt t]
                            add another agent to an existing workgroup (within its repos)
  open <id>                 open the dashboard on a workgroup or agent  (alias: switch)
  ls                        list workgroups (with the repos each is limited to) and their agents  (alias: list)
  move <agent> [<root> | --new]
                            move an agent into another workgroup, or a new one of its own
  repos <agent> <repo>...   re-scope an agent to exactly these tracked repos
  grants <coordinator> [--all | --none | repo...]
                            set a coordinator's host-managed repo ceiling
  rename <id> <name>        set a display name (the id is unchanged)
  archive <id> [--force]    drop a session off the active rail  (alias: done)
  unarchive <id>            put an archived session back  (alias: restore)
  recreate <id>             replace one runtime with current access mounts (host only)
  rm <id> [--force]         delete a session, its worktrees and branches  (alias: delete)

Run 'amux workgroup <command> --help' for details.
